<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alpuente</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alpuente is a small town in the mountains of the north-west of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, dominated by the ruins of its castle. After the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> it was the seat of a small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> ruled by the Banu Qasim from about 1009 until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> took it around 1106. Christian Aragon conquered it in the 13th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alpuente.jpg" alt="Alpuente" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: cargus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alpuente.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
